{"step_index":4922,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T13:48:56Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-23T16:48:56+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-23T16:48:56+03:00\nFile Path: `file:///d:/AI_Engineer/Pharmacy-agy/src/match/coordinator.py`\nTotal Lines: 310\nTotal Bytes: 11730\nShowing lines 15 to 90\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n15: \n16: \n17: SYSTEM_PROMPT = \"\"\"You are a pharmaceutical matching assistant.\n18: Compare requested pharmaceutical product descriptions with a supplied catalog.\n19: \n20: Return ONLY a valid JSON object matching this exact schema:\n21: {\n22:   \"results\": [\n23:     {\n24:       \"case_id\": \"string\",\n25:       \"status\": \"match or no_match or review\",\n26:       \"item_ids\": [\"string\"]\n27:     }\n28:   ]\n29: }\n30: \n31: Rules:\n32: 1. \"match\" means the exact same product, strength, dosage form, and pack size. Return the ID in \"item_ids\".\n33: 2. \"no_match\" means no exact or highly plausible match exists. \"item_ids\" must be empty [].\n34: 3. \"review\" means there is a plausible candidate but details are ambiguous or slightly mismatched.\n35: 4. DO NOT return markdown blocks. Return ONLY the raw JSON starting with { and ending with }.\n36: 5. ONLY return results for cases you are provided.\n37: \"\"\"\n38: \n39: \n40: class Coordinator:\n41:     def __init__(self, config: Config):\n42:         self.config = config\n43:         self.openrouter_api_key = getattr(config, 'openrouter_api_key', None)\n44: \n45:     def process(\n46:         self,\n47:         shortage_items: list[dict],\n48:         warehouse_data: dict[str, list[dict]],\n49:     ) -> dict:\n50:         \n51:         unique_shortages = {}\n52:         for item in shortage_items:\n53:             name = item.get(\"item_name_raw\", \"\")\n54:             if name and name not in unique_shortages:\n55:                 unique_shortages[name] = item\n56:                 \n57:         deduped_shortages = list(unique_shortages.values())\n58: \n59:         print(f\"\\n{'='*60}\")\n60:         print(f\"[*] Starting Match: {len(shortage_items)} raw -> {len(deduped_shortages)} UNIQUE shortages x {len(warehouse_data)} warehouses\")\n61:         print(f\"{'='*60}\\n\")\n62: \n63:         all_warehouse_results = {}\n64:         found_in: dict[str, list[str]] = {}\n65: \n66:         for wh_name, wh_items in warehouse_data.items():\n67:             print(f\"\\n{'-'*40}\")\n68:             print(f\"[Warehouse] {wh_name} ({len(wh_items)} items)\")\n69:             print(f\"{'-'*40}\")\n70: \n71:             wh_result = self._match_warehouse(deduped_shortages, wh_items, wh_name)\n72:             all_warehouse_results[wh_name] = wh_result\n73: \n74:             for match in wh_result[\"matched\"]:\n75:                 name = match[\"shortage_item\"]\n76:                 found_in.setdefault(name, []).append(wh_name)\n77: \n78:         all_shortage_names = {item[\"item_name_raw\"] for item in deduped_shortages}\n79:         found_names = set(found_in.keys())\n80:         \n81:         review_only_names = set()\n82:         for wh_result in all_warehouse_results.values():\n83:             for rev in wh_result[\"needs_review\"]:\n84:                 review_only_names.add(rev[\"shortage_item\"])\n85: \n86:         not_found_names = all_shortage_names - found_names - review_only_names\n87:         not_found_items = [\n88:             {\"name\": name, \"source\": next(\n89:                 (item.get(\"source_file\", \"\") for item in deduped_shortages\n90:                  if item.get(\"item_name_raw\") == name), \"\"\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those line